WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:03.190
Tough times sometimes call for tough measures.

00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:07.520
Since MGM announced that No Time to Die was
pushing its April 2020 release date back to

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:12.600
November due to concerns about the coronavirus
outbreak, film exhibitors everywhere have

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:15.000
grown nervous about when and where the other
shoe will drop.

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:19.960
It's rather a lose-lose situation as it stands
right now, no matter what route is chosen,

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:25.199
as U.S. theater patronage could possibly fall
precipitously by the time the next major blockbuster

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.550
release, Black Widow, is slated to arrive
in theaters.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:31.720
The current conversation regarding potential
release date delays has some speculating that

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:36.571
Disney and Marvel Studios will push the film
from its scheduled May 1 debut, according

00:00:36.571 --> 00:00:40.820
to Deadline. The outlet notes that, quote,
"it wouldn't be jawdropping if Disney decides

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:45.420
to move Black Widow," but there are some tricky
logistics to discuss. Sounds like a real party,

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:45.920
huh?

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:48.300
"I — I don't see how that's a party."

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:53.170
Asian market box office revenue is important
to the franchise's success, and the coronavirus

00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:58.559
situation in China and Korea in particular
is especially concerning for turnout. However,

00:00:58.559 --> 00:01:02.489
moving the release of Black Widow in hopes
of deferring interruption by the coronavirus

00:01:02.489 --> 00:01:06.450
is an expensive and potentially confusing
effort for the consumer base that may not

00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:10.050
be paying attention to shifts in the film
release schedule and may not show up when

00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:14.690
the new release date comes around. The coronavirus
has the potential to be a seasonal event like

00:01:14.690 --> 00:01:18.720
influenza, even though time will certainly
provide more treatment options while global

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:23.080
efforts work hard to find them. One exhibitor
was quoted by Deadline as saying, "we are

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:24.360
in uncharted territory.".

00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:29.080
So far, Disney has decided to stay its course
for Black Widow's May 1 release date. A Bond

00:01:29.090 --> 00:01:32.930
movie changing release date is a big deal,
what with the guaranteed glitz and glamour

00:01:32.930 --> 00:01:37.990
of a red carpet party attached to every continental
premiere, but No Time to Die isn't the marketing

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:40.410
behemoth that any Marvel Cinematic Universe
movie is.

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:45.010
Yes, Black Widow was a surprise inclusion
to the expanding post-Avengers: Endgame universe,

00:01:45.010 --> 00:01:49.360
given that the character died during Endgame
after throwing herself off the cliff in Vormir

00:01:49.490 --> 00:01:53.460
in order for her fellow Avenger Hawkeye to
obtain the Soul Stone and undo the events

00:01:53.470 --> 00:01:58.130
of Avengers: Infinity War. But no MCU film
release is just about the movie. It's also

00:01:58.130 --> 00:02:02.210
about expensive brand tie-ins, like putting
Black Widow actress Scarlett Johansson on

00:02:02.210 --> 00:02:07.090
soda cans and Dorito chip bags. It's about
toys. It also involves the rest of Marvel's

00:02:07.090 --> 00:02:09.979
Phase 4 movie schedule inching along behind
it.

00:02:09.979 --> 00:02:14.340
In other words, Black Widow is more than just
a single movie right now, it's the first car

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:18.740
of a whole train, staring down an economic
hazard that has potential to cause a major

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:23.000
derailment. In that sense, it might be safer
to just release the movie as planned, and

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:27.900
deal with screening it in empty theaters while
hoping to recoup costs via other avenues later.

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:31.671
Another thing worth noting which might indicate
Black Widow sticking to its planned release

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:36.720
date is that Disney and Marvel Studios can
take a financial hit in a way MGM just can't.

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:41.560
No Time to Die will probably be MGM's biggest
box office draw of the year, and the possibility

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:46.070
of releasing it in China specifically when
quarantines and mandatory self-isolation orders

00:02:46.070 --> 00:02:52.130
are in effect means guaranteed major financial
loss. Disney faces similar difficulty in releasing

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:56.400
internationally, but it's also a vastly larger
corporation than MGM, with plenty of other

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:00.760
major releases set to come out over the rest
of the year including, of course, the other

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:02.800
major MCU release, The Eternals.

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:07.480
In related recent news, Marvel Studios has
halted production on its Disney+ series The

00:03:07.490 --> 00:03:12.819
Falcon and the Winter Soldier due to coronavirus
concerns. The show, which stars Anthony Mackie

00:03:12.819 --> 00:03:17.260
and Sebastian Stan in the title roles, was
filming in Prague at the time of the production

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:21.370
shutdown. According to Deadline, The Falcon
and the Winter Soldier had moved production

00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:25.820
from Atlanta to the European country for a
"short shoot" that began on Friday, March

00:03:25.820 --> 00:03:31.569
6, and was expected to be completed in around
one week. On Wednesday, March 11, Marvel executives

00:03:31.569 --> 00:03:35.760
sent everyone out of Prague and back to Atlanta,
with the chances of returning to Prague to

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:38.300
finish the shoot apparently seeming unlikely.

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:42.340
The good news is that Disney and Marvel have
the freedom to put off their unfinished projects

00:03:42.350 --> 00:03:47.100
without too much concern for major consequences;
in the case of Black Widow, it's understandable

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:48.820
that the studios would want to stick to the
plan.

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:52.880
All studios are likely going to wince and
preemptively tighten the projected earning

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:57.510
belt buckle this year due to the coronavirus
outbreak, but at this point in time, there's

00:03:57.510 --> 00:04:01.750
no real reason to worry about Black Widow's
fate. Whatever happens, we're sure we'll see

00:04:01.750 --> 00:04:02.460
it eventually.

